Z||000000||BAM-BAM||10-15-2000||01:25 AM||||  I was trying to post a picture of my new steering wheel on a previous post. Every time I tried, I got a successful upload, then when I would hit control V it would apply something completely different. Why is this? I read a post the other day where some one else was having the same problem. HELP! I'm CONFUSED!!!!<P><BR> Thanks, BAM-BAM!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||10-15-2000||04:42 AM||||PIP copies the UBB code to include in your message to the clipboard (hence the CTRL-V). If some other program writes something to the clipboard after you have uploaded the image, then that UBB code is lost. What you could try is this: just write your message, and when it is time to insert an (already uploaded) image, go to PIP, click "History", find the image you want to insert, and click the button below the thumbnail (the button that holds the image's filename). At the bottom of the History window you should see the UBB code appear. Now switch to your browser window and press CTRL-V inside your message.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||10-15-2000||11:02 AM||||  Cliff, what I did was alost the same as you had said, the only difference is that I got the UBB code in the viewbar and highlighted it, right mouse clicked and chose copy, then I inserted it and it worked. Before that I had even tried shutting my computer down and nothing worked. I kept gettin the same message insert that I had posted earlier in a post to Monkeyman. It was an E-Bay shortcut. Maybe that had something to do with it. <BR>Thanks Cliff.<P> Later, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-15-2000||11:23 AM||||Something to also keep in mind.... Win98 running Office 2K product, at least I think its done by Office, gets an upgraded clipboard. It can now hold multiple items in the que. This can sometimes produce strange results on paste. I don't have all the details. I just noticed this a few days ago and haven't had time to dig into it much. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||10-15-2000||06:40 PM||||I have that problem too. Even after I upload a picture and get the successfully uploaded message, it still doesnt copy to the clipboard. I have to go to History, click the address of the picture I want and then select it and copy it. Always works for me. Not to much trouble. <P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
